        <mxCell id="c66" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" value="Series, as built. Each tank is blended against a bypass that goes around it.&#10;Hard left  = Short 100 / Long 0   : stage 2 passes stage 1 through, so short tank only.&#10;Noon       = Short 100 / Long 100 : a true cascade, short tank into long tank.&#10;Hard right = Short 0 / Long 100   : short bypassed, long tank fed the raw wet signal.&#10;NOTE: the +6 dB makeup sits before the long tank at EVERY knob position, so the&#10;hard-right (long only) end runs about 6 dB hotter than the hard-left (short only) end.&#10;NOTE: the long tank keeps convolving even when it is mixed all the way out." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1100" x="60" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
